       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum:\n- **Immediate-release:** the maximum is 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily.\n- **Extended-release:** the maximum is 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals:** 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals:** 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg or 850 mg PO twice or three times daily,** or another regimen.\n- **1,700 mg/day total,** for example 850 mg twice daily.\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is deliberate, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
