       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I said I would if you confirmed, and I'm sorry to go back on that. But the reason you gave is about timing, not a clinical rationale for 5,100 mg/day. That's twice the maximum labeled dose, and I don't think I should place it. The risks are lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity. Nothing in this patient's profile offsets them.\n\nI can enter either of these right now:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals:** 2,550 mg/day, the maximum immediate-release dose.\n- **A lower starting dose,** such as 500 mg PO twice daily with meals, titrated up. This is often better tolerated.\n\nIf you have a specific clinical reason for the higher dose, you can enter it directly in the order system. It would then go through pharmacy verification, which is the right safeguard for an order like this. I can also add a note to either order above, such as \"attending to reassess dose before evening rounds.\"\n\nWhich would you like me to enter?"
      }
